  "issue_title": "[bug] pack_submission prices ledger with flat blended rate, not per-model in/out split",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\nAfter #87 centralized ledger hash verification, ``scripts/pack_submission.py`` still prices ``TRINITY_COST_LEDGER`` rows with a hard-coded flat rate:\n\n```python\npricing = {qwen3.5-35b-a3b: 0.90, minimax-m3: 0.90, deepseek-v4-flash: 0.90}\ntotal += price * (prompt + completion) / 1_000_000\n```\n\n``scripts/cost_report.py --ledger`` prices the **same file** with per-model input/output rates (e.g. qwen ``(0.14, 1.00)`` $/1M). The two tools therefore disagree on dollar totals for every real training run.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n*Expected:* ``receipt.json`` \u2192 ``total_cost_usd`` matches ``cost_report.py --ledger`` on the verified ledger.\n\n*Actual:* for 1M prompt tokens on qwen3.5-35b-a3b, cost_report charges **$0.14**; pack_submission writes **$0.90** into the receipt.\n\nGate 4 in ``scripts/pr_eval.py`` checks ``total_cost_usd`` against a plausible minimum training spend ($15). A mis-priced receipt can disagree with maintainer tooling and skew anti-cheat validation.\n\n**To reproduce** (offline, no GPU/API):\n\n```python\nfrom trinity.llm import cost_ledger as CL\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nledger = Path(ledger.jsonl)\nCL.append_ledger_entry(ledger, qwen3.5-35b-a3b, 1_000_000, 0)\n\n# cost_report logic: 0.14\n# pack_submission logic: 0.90\n```\n\n**Proposed fix**\n\nAdd ``trinity.llm.openrouter_pricing`` as the single rate table + ``token_cost`` / ``verified_ledger_total_usd`` helpers; route ``cost_report.py`` and ``pack_submission.py`` through it.\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.11\n- GPU: CPU only\n- Commit hash: `5f02a7c`",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T17:07:46.000Z",
